scripts/check-generated-tree-freshness.mjs is the one staleness predicate for the committed generated trees — modified, untracked, and deleted paths all count — and every caller reaches it through the one gate-set definition in scripts/run-pipeline-gates.sh (its generated-trees phase): validate.sh, ci.yml's pipeline-gates job, and the release workflow all execute that phase rather than hand-rolled git checks or hand-copied gate lists; a caller that measures with its own git predicate — or names individual gate scripts instead of the shared phase — reintroduces the local-green/CI-red divergence the predicate exists to prevent. The gate holds no hand-maintained tree enumeration: the skills trees derive from the registry and the hook trees are observed by replaying the agent-hooks build scripts into scratch directories, reconciled both ways against the registry's platform set and the working tree, so a renamed build destination or an unbuilt platform goes red instead of dropping out of measurement; its failure text branches on the build driver's exit-code contract so each reachable cause reads differently.
